": "A time-ignoring path 798-389-131 exists via the very high-degree hub 389, but no 798-389 interaction occurs in the time bands adjacent to 131's incoming events (steps 14,15), and 798's only other activity (~11000) precedes 131's next reception by >2400 units, exceeding the 600-unit relay limit. 798's final event postdates 131's final event. Alternative relays into 131 are also excluded: 368 and 972 are inactive in the critical interval, 1877 has zero in-degree over the whole window (cannot relay), and 1932's in-neighbours are disjoint from 798's contacts. The apparent link is driven by hub popularity and aggregate volume, not by any time-respecting sequence."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static connectivity exists, but that's the confound.** Node 798's out-neighbours are {45, 132, 389} (step_03) and 131's in-neighbours are {368, 972, 1877, 1932} (step_04). The 2-hop subgraph (step_05) contains the edges 798\u2013389 and 389\u2192131, so an *order-ignoring* path 798\u2192389\u2192131 exists. Node 389 is a massive hub (hundreds of edges; 21 events in a 3,000-unit slice, step_16) \u2014 exactly the kind of structure that manufactures spurious \"connections.\"\n\n**Temporal test fails.**\n- 798 fires only in 4 narrow bands: ~[10903,11502] (2 ev), [23503,24102] (1), [25303,25902] (1), [33103,37902] (1) (steps 09, 12).\n- 131 receives only at ~[10303,10902], [13903,18702], [18703,23502], [24703,25302], [25903,26502], [28303,33102] (steps 10, 13).\n- The only 131 activity within reach of 798's mid-window bursts is at [24703,25302] and [25903,26502]. Checking the hub relay directly: **no 798\u2194389 event occurs in [23503,24102] or [25303,25902]** (steps 14, 15). So the hub path is unusable at precisely the times it would be needed.\n- 798's remaining events at ~11000 are followed by *no* 131 event until \u226513903 \u2014 a gap \u22652,400 units, far beyond the 600-unit relay budget for a short chain.\n- 798's last event (\u226533103) comes after 131's last event (\u226433102), so it cannot influence 131 at all.\n- Alternative relays are dead: 368 and 972 are completely silent in [23503,26502] (step_16), and 1877 has **in-degree 0** across the entire window (step_08), so it can never have received influence to pass on. 1932's in-neighbours {435,1440,1450,1747,1887,1916} (step_11) include none of 798's contacts.\n\n**Conclusion: the connection is structural, not temporal.**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_6f333458\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131, 389, 1877, 1932, 368, 972],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.72,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A time-ignoring path 798-389-131 exists via the very high-degree hub 389, but no 798-389 interaction occurs in the time bands adjacent to 131's incoming events (steps 14,15), and 798's only other activity (~11000) precedes 131's next reception by >2400 units, exceeding the 600-unit relay limit. 798's final event postdates 131's final event. Alternative relays into 131 are also excluded: 368 and 972 are inactive in the critical interval, 1877 has zero in-degree over the whole window (cannot relay), and 1932's in-neighbours are disjoint from 798's contacts. The apparent link is driven by hub popularity and aggregate volume, not by any time-respecting sequence.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 35004, "total_output_tokens": 10797, "total_tokens": 45801, "total_latency_ms": 138337, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}